WEBVTT

00:00:00.782 --> 00:00:02.307
Your patents aren't the problem.

00:00:02.941 --> 00:00:03.881
Your tools are.

00:00:04.301 --> 00:00:05.722
Deadlines in a spreadsheet.

00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:07.602
Filings buried in email.

00:00:08.023 --> 00:00:09.223
Drafts in Word,

00:00:09.523 --> 00:00:11.984
and prior art scattered across a dozen tabs

00:00:12.004 --> 00:00:13.604
and multiple patent offices.

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.945
One missed annuity, one blown office action,

00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:19.866
and a patent you spent years on quietly lapses.

00:00:20.406 --> 00:00:22.087
This is Design Your Invention.

00:00:22.547 --> 00:00:24.888
One platform that replaces your spreadsheets,

00:00:25.088 --> 00:00:28.449
your scattered searches, and your drafting and response tools.

00:00:29.391 --> 00:00:32.032
Patent operations all begin in one place.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.073
The whole portfolio, on a single dashboard.

00:00:35.673 --> 00:00:37.494
Deadlines, ranked by risk.

00:00:38.254 --> 00:00:40.875
NPE cases, ready to triage.

00:00:41.535 --> 00:00:44.095
Office actions, tracked to every date.

00:00:44.556 --> 00:00:47.657
Annuity fees, scheduled across jurisdictions.

00:00:48.157 --> 00:00:50.978
And a full audit log, recording every change.

00:00:51.447 --> 00:00:54.889
One search across more than 100 patent jurisdictions,

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.332
with full claims from the USPTO

00:00:57.652 --> 00:00:58.493
and the EPO.

00:00:59.874 --> 00:01:00.955
Open any patent,

00:01:01.135 --> 00:01:02.856
and we enrich it with compound data

00:01:02.876 --> 00:01:04.898
from ChEMBL and PubChem,

00:01:05.759 --> 00:01:07.780
and link it to live clinical trials.

00:01:08.881 --> 00:01:11.463
From your invention and the prior art you saved,

00:01:11.743 --> 00:01:14.605
generate a first draft, ready for attorney review.

00:01:16.146 --> 00:01:18.007
Independent and dependent claims,

00:01:18.368 --> 00:01:20.949
an abstract and a full specification,

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.011
written for the USPTO,

00:01:23.411 --> 00:01:25.292
the EPO, and beyond.

00:01:25.953 --> 00:01:28.054
Every claim is scored for confidence

00:01:28.214 --> 00:01:30.015
and checked against your prior art.

00:01:30.616 --> 00:01:32.697
Refine any claim in plain English,

00:01:32.777 --> 00:01:35.099
and approve all under attorney review.

00:01:35.879 --> 00:01:37.280
The attorney is the author,

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.282
and the AI is the assistant.

00:01:39.809 --> 00:01:42.111
Then the USPTO pushes back.

00:01:42.671 --> 00:01:44.872
Every rejection is mapped to your claims,

00:01:45.013 --> 00:01:47.534
and every quote is checked against its source.

00:01:48.195 --> 00:01:50.796
An attorney signs off, picks a strategy,

00:01:51.076 --> 00:01:53.358
and amends with support from the application.

00:01:54.098 --> 00:01:55.619
A second attorney approves,

00:01:55.779 --> 00:01:57.320
and the filing copy is ready.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:02.602
Behind every patent is confidential data.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.245
So we protect it on all six sides:

00:02:05.685 --> 00:02:08.388
row-level security, tenant isolation,

00:02:08.848 --> 00:02:11.951
append-only audit trails, granular roles,

00:02:12.391 --> 00:02:13.932
enterprise single sign-on,

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.375
and confidential AI processing.

00:02:17.115 --> 00:02:19.097
Six layers, one sealed core,

00:02:19.317 --> 00:02:22.300
with controls aligned to 21 CFR Part 11.

00:02:23.441 --> 00:02:25.903
Across more than 100 patent jurisdictions,

00:02:26.263 --> 00:02:27.604
built for IP teams.

00:02:28.044 --> 00:02:29.265
Design Your Invention.

00:02:29.665 --> 00:02:32.347
Your IP operations, all in one place.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:33.908
Book a demo today.
